{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes","id":1275442,"title":"DrLoveMonkey's Review of DB Changes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-19T21:27:54-08:00","id":1275442,"title":"DrLoveMonkey's Review of DB Changes","content":"Okay, so first off, here's the list that I compiled. I didn't do this with any software so expect there to be some missing charms, but I think I got more than I missed. Anyone who notices any more please post and I'll update the list.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Archery</b><br /> <br /> Credit to Parabola for finding these ones<ul><li>Unobstructed Hunter's Aim, the excellency, has improved its secondary effect from 'as long as you attack a living or undead target, ignore one point of penalty from visual obstruction' to the same, but every added die ignores one point of such penalties.</li> <li>Sky-Calming Draw went from 4m to 3m, and changed &quot;In Air Aura, the Dragon-Blood may use this Charm without needing to aim beforehand&quot; to &quot;If her weapon already has long range, she instead adds an automatic success on the attack roll&quot;.</li> <li>Death From Nowhere went from 3m to 4m, but you don't need to spend a round aiming before using it, and if you did aim beforehand, you ignore (higher of Essence or Perception) soak, instead of (lower of Essence or Perception).</li> <li>Life-Swelling Sap Strike's 1wp cost is now an optional surcharge when used against undead, to ensure they are incapacitated if crashed. The surcharge is waived if used against trivial foes (!).</li> <li>Arbor Sentinel Technique no longer requires 1wp to use.</li> <li>Spring Follows Winter has been heavily changed. The cost has been reduced from 5m, 2i, to 2m (+1i per die). Instead of being 'make a decisive attack, roll twice and use the better result', you can reroll non-1 failures for one Initiative each (the initiative isnt paid until after the roll).</li> <li>Horizon-Spanning Arc is now once-per-scene, reset by crashing an enemy whose initiative was higher than yours.</li> <li>Seven-Year Swarm Volley and Swallows Defend the Nest have changed names for some reason.</li> </ul><b>Athletics</b><ul><li>Strength of Stone Technique's cost changed from 1m, 1wp to 5m</li> <li>Graceful Dryad Dance now allows you to move down as well as up</li> </ul><b>Awareness</b><ul><li>Sense-Riding Technique now ends if the target gets more than (Essence * 5) miles away.</li> </ul><b>Brawl</b><ul><li>Oaken Thew Exertion had it's cost lowered from 5 to 4 motes</li> <li>Blade Deflecting Palm had it's price lowered from 4m 1i to being able to pay for the reroll 1m per die, plus the initiative. It also lost the water aura effect of onslaught reducing the charms cost by mote. It is now essence 2 and can be used after the attack.</li> <li>Stone Fist Strike added an extra effect where it now grants your unarmed attacks the smashing keyword, and that effect can be applied to decisive attacks.</li> <li>Firmament-Shattering Impact changed it's name to Crater Making Impact</li> </ul><b>Craft</b><ul><li>Blazing Dragon Smith Arete now rolls an additional non-charm die for every 10</li> <li>Imago-Hatching Realization can only be used once per project, but the &quot;unexpected but useful feature&quot; only requires the rerolled dice to yield a success instead of having to turn the roll itself from a failure into a success.</li> </ul><b>Dodge</b><ul><li>Ember Amid-Smoke Misdirection went from 3m2i to 3m in cost</li> <li>Unassailable Body of Fire had it's counterattack damage increased from (Evasion/2) to (Essence + Evasion)/2.</li> <li>Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion now makes Unassailable Body of Fire and Hopping Firecracker Evasion into whatever element your aura curently is.</li> <li>Unmoving Center of Enlightenment can now be resisted for 5i 1wp</li> </ul><b>Medicine</b><ul><li>Constitution-Tempering Discipline became Indomitable Vitality Discipline.</li> </ul><b>Melee</b><ul><li>Buring Fury Wreath has an added bonus, in fire aura the effect is doubled.</li> <li>Flame-Borne Interception's cost inceased by 1 mote, but now it's a turn long +1 parry, that in addition increases your parry for each successfully blocked attack</li> <li>Harnessed Firestorm Assault now uses higher of Dex or Str, and excellencies only need be paid for once for all attacks</li> <li>Dragon Soul Burst changed cost from 5m 3i to 8m</li> <li>Mela's Flashing Tongue now has a maximum number of attacks equal to (Dex + Str)</li> </ul><b>Sail</b><ul><li>Old Salt Spirit's cost was reduced from 5m 1wp, to 5m.</li> </ul><b>Thrown</b><ul><li>Hundred Thorns Blossom had it's cost reduced from 10m,3i,1wp to 5m,3i,1wp</li> </ul><b>Martial Arts</b><ul><li>Bottomless Depths Defense is now only usable on decisive attacks, and must be declared before the attack is rolled, which I believe is normal for defensive charms anyway.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Formatting Errors</b><br /> <br /> Dodge: Ember Amid Smoke Misdirection<br /> Ride: Small formatting error in<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In addition to that we have 5 free excellencies right off chargen, a much lower xp requirement for essence 3, and none of the trees have excellency requirements anymore. The 5 free excellencies is good, I do recall some early character designs that I came up with felt a bit slow to start, and this will help with that. If you consider that DBs get a 2 for 1 effect with all their excellencies, this almost gives them 20 charms off chargen, which is impressive.<br /> <br /> The lack of pre-requisites is also a good thing. Sometimes you just want Spirit Detecting Mirror technique for your ghostbuster, but you don't necessarily need her to be the most adept at all things occult. Or maybe you just want Wind-Carried Words technique to be able to communicate with your squad, whatever the case is, it's helpful. Also in my experience games tend to last almost as long as it took to get to essence 3, so I was thinking about signature charms more as the final powers you'd get in a campaign before the end, but now they can feel more natural to your character progression, which is good.<br /> <br /> Otherwise the changes just seem good. There's a few charms that I think missed a bit of a buff that maybe should have gotten it, but otherwise things like Flame Borne Interception, and Oaken Thew Exertion got what they needed. The former is now at least breaks even if you get attacked twice and fail to parry the first attack, and goes up from there. Harnessed Firestorm Assault is now useful even if you have low dex, just as long as you don't have low strength too, and at that point you're probably not really that much of a swordsperson. Stone Fist Strike giving a smash attack makes it a much cooler charm as well as enables Rolling Boulder Blow, which was a bit of an oversight before I think that you needed a weapon to do it.<br /> <br /> Then there's just a few changes to things like Mela's Flashing Tongue and Sense Riding having some kind of cap, which before probably hardly came up but really they should have one. Overall though from my first glances, I think it looks good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 01-16-2019, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T01:57:20-08:00","id":1275456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes#post1275442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so first off, here's the list that I compiled. I didn't do this with any software so expect there to be some missing charms, but I think I got more than I missed. Anyone who notices any more please post and I'll update the list.<br /> <br /> ...[*]Blade Deflecting Palm had it's price lowered from 4m 1i to being able to pay for the reroll 1m per die, plus the initiative. It also lost the water aura effect of onslaught reducing the charms cost by mote.</div> </div> </div> </div>One I noticed and appreciated is that Blade Deflecting Palm is now used after the attack. It's a pretty good Charm now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T03:23:41-08:00","id":1275462,"title":"","content":"It's also essence 2 instead of essence 1.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T06:07:33-08:00","id":1275482,"title":"","content":"About not needing excellencies, their benefits when you have, say, skill 1 and no specialties, are extremely slight for a full-charm buy. It's much better than you can opt-in when you will get some benefit out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T06:39:50-08:00","id":1275488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275482#post1275482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About not needing excellencies, their benefits when you have, say, skill 1 and no specialties, are extremely slight for a full-charm buy. It's much better than you can opt-in when you will get some benefit out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, it\u2019s less so for Solars because they always get their attribute added to the dicecap as well, and their charms also tend to have less unique and self contained effects. Like getting double 9s on a linguistics roll when you\u2019re not good at linguistics is meh, but being able to communicate over miles instantly is always good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:08:15-08:00","id":1275498,"title":"","content":"What do people think of the return to rounding down for static value increases from excellencies? I know it was always intended to work that way, but it is a pretty significant nerf to the Melee, Brawl, Dodge, Integrity and Socialise excellencies.<br /> Specialties are much more important because of it.<br /> <br /> It is, though, more consistent with the rest of the line. And by rewarding 5s less, might mean less min-maxed characters happy with Dodge 4.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I've historically found it difficult to get players to remember that static value caps round down, as they assume everything rounds up for Exalts, so having DBs round up would have been easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-20-2018, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:28:46-08:00","id":1275504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275498#post1275498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do people think of the return to rounding down for static value increases from excellencies? I know it was always intended to work that way, but it is a pretty significant nerf to the Melee, Brawl, Dodge, Integrity and Socialise excellencies.<br /> Specialties are much more important because of it.<br /> <br /> It is, though, more consistent with the rest of the line. And by rewarding 5s less, might mean less min-maxed characters happy with Dodge 4.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I've historically found it difficult to get players to remember that static value caps round down, as they assume everything rounds up for Exalts, so having DBs round up would have been easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m afraid I don\u2019t understand. I\u2019m looking at the charm section right now and it says for static values you can raise them by \u201cno more than half this amount, rounded up.\u201d And then gives an example showing that with a specialty putting your cap to 5, you may raise the static value by 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T08:07:20-08:00","id":1275518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275504#post1275504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m afraid I don\u2019t understand. I\u2019m looking at the charm section right now and it says for static values you can raise them by \u201cno more than half this amount, rounded up.\u201d And then gives an example showing that with a specialty putting your cap to 5, you may raise the static value by 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1275486#post1275486\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1275486#post1275486\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1275486#post1275486\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1275486#post1275486 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T08:08:57-08:00","id":1275519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275504#post1275504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m afraid I don\u2019t understand. I\u2019m looking at the charm section right now and it says for static values you can raise them by \u201cno more than half this amount, rounded up.\u201d And then gives an example showing that with a specialty putting your cap to 5, you may raise the static value by 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance just corrected that in the Ask the Devs thread, asking it to be put in the DB errata thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T09:12:52-08:00","id":1275533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275498#post1275498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do people think of the return to rounding down for static value increases from excellencies? I know it was always intended to work that way, but it is a pretty significant nerf to the Melee, Brawl, Dodge, Integrity and Socialise excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's unfortunate and going to lead to specialties like &quot;when joining battle&quot; because of how much you potentially lose by not having them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T09:16:42-08:00","id":1275535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275519#post1275519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vance just corrected that in the Ask the Devs thread, asking it to be put in the DB errata thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Jesus whiplash. <br /> <br /> \u201cWait DBs round down again? Hang on DBs used to round up? Wait do Solars round up!?\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t personally have much of an opinion on it. It doesn\u2019t affect the min-maxers much since they\u2019d have 6 dice there either way. I think I probably prefer it rounding down? I find usually players have max in a lot of abilities anyway, not just for minmaxing but because of charm requirements, and this makes having an applicable specialty a bit more meaningful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T09:20:14-08:00","id":1275536,"title":"","content":"I'm disappointed that Shimmering Heat-Mirage Tactic is still a trap pick, but otherwise like the changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T09:32:12-08:00","id":1275539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275498#post1275498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do people think of the return to rounding down for static value increases from excellencies? I know it was always intended to work that way, but it is a pretty significant nerf to the Melee, Brawl, Dodge, Integrity and Socialise excellencies.<br /> Specialties are much more important because of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never realized they were written that way in the first place, so it's not much of a change for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T09:56:40-08:00","id":1275545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275536#post1275536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm disappointed that Shimmering Heat-Mirage Tactic is still a trap pick, but otherwise like the changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was on the lookout for that one as well, and I\u2019m still not sure about it. Like if you\u2019re in Fire Aura tue effect only drops if they roll no ones and roll at least one ten, which is not wretched odds. It also doesn\u2019t risk being dropped by trivial opponents, who looking at the sidebar for I\u2019m not 100% sure I\u2019ve even used correctly in the past.<br /> <br /> Then again it\u2019s a simple charm, so your giving up your turn to activate it, that\u2019s a pretty big cost. It\u2019s probably meant to be used after you get caught sneaking and are running away, dodging the arrows of the house guards or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T10:04:06-08:00","id":1275547,"title":"","content":"If it were reflexive the risk and initiative cost would be worth it. As a simple it's just overpriced and weaker Full Defense that *might* last an extra round or two but also costs against your charm cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T15:50:20-08:00","id":1275650,"title":"","content":"Can Blade-Deflecting Palm be used with Martial Arts parries? I don't remember if Vance said the kickstarter copy was in error about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T16:19:20-08:00","id":1275655,"title":"","content":"It still says &quot;brawl or martial arts&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T06:16:16-08:00","id":1275779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275498#post1275498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do people think of the return to rounding down for static value increases from excellencies? I know it was always intended to work that way, but it is a pretty significant nerf to the Melee, Brawl, Dodge, Integrity and Socialise excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a terrible change but the upside is that now I have absolutely no reservations about houseruling that static values and success adders <i>both</i> round up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T10:10:02-08:00","id":1275835,"title":"","content":"For Solars and Lunars as well?<br /> <br /> TBH, I find that Exalted has a bit of an issue with PCs having 5s all over the place. So by reducing the benefit of 5s a bit in relation to 4s, maybe I'll see more PCs with a bunch of 4s than a bunch of 5s. The main problem I foresee is not balance (I think it's fine for that) but players constantly forgetting how it works, or, as Lioness mentioned, picking boring specialties for Dodge and Melee (but then, they were probably always going to do that, tbh).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T12:11:19-08:00","id":1275862,"title":"","content":"Did Graceful Dryad Dance get that buff Vance he'd add?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T13:27:50-08:00","id":1275877,"title":"","content":"What buff?<br /> The only change I see is before it let you move up or down 2 range bands, and now it lets you move up or down 1 or 2 range bands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T13:39:20-08:00","id":1275880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275835#post1275835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBH, I find that Exalted has a bit of an issue with PCs having 5s all over the place. So by reducing the benefit of 5s a bit in relation to 4s, maybe I'll see more PCs with a bunch of 4s than a bunch of 5s. The main problem I foresee is not balance (I think it's fine for that) but players constantly forgetting how it works, or, as Lioness mentioned, picking boring specialties for Dodge and Melee (but then, they were probably always going to do that, tbh).</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, because to me, the change seems to incentivize the opposite: whereas you could get away with having 4+specialty before and sit secure in the knowledge that you may not be optimal, but you still have your full defensive power budget to rely on if shit hits the fan, now it's 5+spec or you lose out on a third of your supernatural potential.<br /> <br /> That said, after checking the math, the change definitely seems to be better for combat flow: rounding up <i>twice</i> plus having a medium weapon means that in a fight between two equally asymmetrically skilled combatants, the defender has an effective +2 bonus if both of them go all-out, which means that the chances of connecting with a decisive end up somewhere in the realm of &lt;30% instead of the much more reasonable ~40% that round down results in. (However, I maintain that the original sin in this case is in allowing the defense bonus from medium weapons to apply on decisives, and warping the game's incentives to even more disproportionally favor creating flawlessly minmaxed superbeings is not a good thing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T14:10:17-08:00","id":1275892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275877#post1275877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What buff?<br /> The only change I see is before it let you move up or down 2 range bands, and now it lets you move up or down 1 or 2 range bands.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't used to allow you to move down two range bands.<br /> <br /> I asked Vance if it made sense that it would or should allow you to safely descend two range bands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T01:24:20-08:00","id":1276029,"title":"","content":"Ah, sure.<br /> <br /> Any other changes anyone's noticed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T04:15:27-08:00","id":1276033,"title":"","content":"Bottomless Depths Defense got a nerf but it's more like a slap on the wrist, it's still very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T07:46:49-08:00","id":1276045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1275835#post1275835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(but then, they were probably always going to do that, tbh)</div> </div> </div> </div>For the abilities people use in combat, yes.<br /> <br /> People were going to take &quot;Specialty (the weapon type I always use)&quot; and this ruling doesn't change anything on the ground because people generally enter into combat on their own terms. But with abilities like Awareness, Integrity and Lore that also add successes, they tend to be things the ST might prompt you to roll/apply without being immediately clear what's going on (often because the roll itself is supposed to tell you that) and not having an applicable specialty there can be hobbling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T01:04:29-08:00","id":1277315,"title":"","content":"Unmoving Center Enlightenment can now be resisted for 5i, 1wp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T10:14:32-08:00","id":1277373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1277315#post1277315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unmoving Center Enlightenment can now be resisted for 5i, 1wp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I\u2019ll update it when I get home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T12:09:58-08:00","id":1280719,"title":"","content":"Blazing Dragon-Smith Arete gives exploding 10s.<br /> <br /> Imago-Hatching Realization can only be used once per project, but the &quot;unexpected but useful feature&quot; only requires the rerolled dice to yield a success instead of having to turn the roll itself from a failure into a success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 01-14-2019, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T11:03:14-08:00","id":1280939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1280719#post1280719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blazing Dragon-Smith Arete gives exploding 10s.<br /> <br /> Imago-Hatching Realization can only be used once per project, but the &quot;unexpected but useful feature&quot; only requires the rerolled dice to yield a success instead of having to turn the roll itself from a failure into a success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Updated! Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T12:15:15-08:00","id":1281150,"title":"","content":"Wait, is Stone Fist Strike no longer Withering-only? If that didn't change, it cannot possibly assist with Decisive-only Rolling Boulder Blow or Firmament-Shattering Strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T12:50:04-08:00","id":1281165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1281150#post1281150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, is Stone Fist Strike no longer Withering-only? If that didn't change, it cannot possibly assist with Decisive-only Rolling Boulder Blow or Firmament-Shattering Strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it is no longer withering only. However the only advantage to a decisive is that it adds the smashing tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T13:39:52-08:00","id":1281172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1281165#post1281165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed it is no longer withering only. However the only advantage to a decisive is that it adds the smashing tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it takes 3m, 2i, and -1 Defense to make a smashing attack. Oh, and breaking any non-Earth Aura.<br /> <br /> Does Earth Aura do anything for decisive uses of the Charm, at least?<br /> <br /> <br /> Does the Charm not grant the possibility of smashing attacks to withering attacks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-16-2019, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T16:18:31-08:00","id":1281205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1281172#post1281172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it takes 3m, 1i, and -1 Defense to make a smashing attack. Oh, and breaking any non-Earth Aura.<br /> <br /> Does Earth Aura do anything for decisive uses of the Charm, at least?<br /> <br /> <br /> Does the Charm not grant the possibility of smashing attacks to withering attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>The charm also grants the smashing tag to withering attacks, but the bonus to the attack roll and, obviously, the overwhelming damage do not apply to decisive attacks. And yes, to make the smashing attack one must still pay the cost of smashing, which is actually -1D and 2i. It can actually be extremely powerful though. Knocking sombody prone makes them take a -1 to Parry and a -2 to Evasion* and then if they want to end that condition they have to flurry, which is a -1 to Defense in general and a -3 to any action they flurry it with. Or they could just waste an entire turn doing nothing but scrambling to their feet, that'd be cool too. <br /> <br /> <br /> *As well as -3 to attacks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T19:37:50-08:00","id":1281240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1281205#post1281205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The charm also grants the smashing tag to withering attacks, but the bonus to the attack roll and, obviously, the overwhelming damage do not apply to decisive attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Overwhelming benefit is pointless, but that doesn't mean any damage bonus is impossible.<br /> <br /> I don't see why the automatic success on the attack roll is incompatible with a decisive attack dice-pool, either. It's not an Accuracy bonus, it's a Charm-die bonus worth two rolled dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> which is actually -1D and 2i. </div> </div> </div>I mistyped.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It can actually be extremely powerful though. </div> </div> </div>I know knocking a target prone is powerful, but you can use the Charm for the same price to do it with a withering attack that will be more accurate from the accuracy bonus and the automatic success.<br /> <br /> You're paying the SAME cost for the decisive attack, but with less effect.<br /> <br /> While decisive smash attacks are still useful, it mostly just ends up being a tax on using Rolling Boulder Blow and Firmament-Shattering Strike barehanded, when either of those Charms could just enable the ability to make smashing attacks (with the usual cost) on their own. Especially FSS, which is a Simple-type Charm to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T21:34:58-08:00","id":1281253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1281240#post1281240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While decisive smash attacks are still useful, it mostly just ends up being a tax on using Rolling Boulder Blow and Firmament-Shattering Strike barehanded, when either of those Charms could just enable the ability to make smashing attacks (with the usual cost) on their own. Especially FSS, which is a Simple-type Charm to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think the effect could definitely stand to get at least the bonus success for decisives. That way it's not 100% just a copy of the excellency, just to be a bit different, and more worth the cost probably? Especially since I'm not sure that any of this can't just be done while wearing a cestus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T12:16:27-08:00","id":1281336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1281253#post1281253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since I'm not sure that any of this can't just be done while wearing a cestus.</div> </div> </div> </div>It totally can! Just a simple, makeshift cestus is all it takes to get the smashing tag on natural Brawl attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T12:27:43-08:00","id":1281341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1275442-drlovemonkey-s-review-of-db-changes?p=1281336#post1281336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It totally can! Just a simple, makeshift cestus is all it takes to get the smashing tag on natural Brawl attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it MIGHT not. Oddly Stone Fist specifies unarmed attack, where looking through the other brawl charms they don\u2019t. Perhaps Stone Fist Strike can only be used while truely unarmed?<br /> <br /> This is important to me as DB brawler is one of my new favourite character concepts. Just something about a magistrate using stone chipping fists and water grapples to kill demons is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T12:45:44-08:00","id":1281351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_post